==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic (corresponding to {{term|dugan}} + {{term|-þ}}).  Cognate with Old Frisian ''[[duged]]'' (Dutch ''[[deugd]]''), Old High German ''[[tugund]]'' (German ''[[Tugend]]''), Old Norse ''[[dygð]]'' (Swedish ''[[dygd]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈduɣuθ/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
'''duguþ''' {{f}}

# band of warriors, [[army]]
# [[prosperity]], [[benefit]]

